---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Back-of-the-envelope numbers" hint="How likely reads and writes are to succeed with a strict quorum and with a sloppy one, how likely a slow replica is to slow a request down, how many keys move when a node joins, and how many requests a day need a merge. A teaching model with round numbers, not Amazon's data.">
  <div class="pg est" data-est>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <RangeField label="Copies of each key (N)" name="n" min="1" max="7" value="3" />
      <RangeField label="Replies a read waits for (R)" name="r" min="1" max="7" value="2" />
      <RangeField label="Acknowledgements a write waits for (W)" name="w" min="1" max="7" value="2" />
      <RangeField label="Chance that a node is unreachable (%)" name="f" min="0" max="20" step="0.5" value="1" />
      <RangeField label="Spare nodes after the first N in the list" name="x" min="0" max="4" value="2" />
      <RangeField label="Chance that a replica is slow (%)" name="p" min="0" max="20" step="0.5" value="1" />
      <RangeField label="Nodes in the ring" name="s" min="3" max="300" value="30" />
      <RangeField label="Requests a day (millions)" name="q" min="1" max="1000" value="100" />
      <RangeField label="Keys in one key range (millions)" name="k" min="1" max="1000" value="10" />
    </div>
    <dl class="est-out" data-out aria-live="polite"></dl>
    <p class="pg-note">Teaching model, not Amazon's system or data. From the paper: the usual setting is N=3, R=2, W=2; a key's list of nodes has spares behind the first N; a node gossips with a random peer every second; and in one 24-hour sample of the shopping cart 99.94% of requests saw one version, 0.00057% saw two, 0.00047% saw three and 0.00009% saw four. The paper gives no failure or slowness probabilities, so those figures are guesses of mine that you can change. Assumptions: nodes fail or run slow independently of one another; a request is slowed when fewer than R (or W) replicas are fast; the keys in a range are spread evenly; and the paper's cart shares are applied to your requests. The gossip estimate is a rough epidemic one, not a figure from the paper.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue, formatOneDecimalBelow100 } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-est]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const OUT_ROWS = 12; // lines in the result list
    const PERCENT = 100, MILLION = 1e6;
    const CART_CONFLICT_PERCENT = 0.00057 + 0.00047 + 0.00009; // shares of requests that saw two, three or four versions, from the paper
    const rows = Array.from({ length: OUT_ROWS }, () => { const dt = document.createElement('dt'); const dd = document.createElement('dd'); q('[data-out]').append(dt, dd); return { dt, dd }; });
    const choose = (n: number, k: number): number => { let c = 1; for (let i = 1; i <= k; i++) c = (c * (n - k + i)) / i; return c; };
    /** The chance that at least `need` of `total` independent nodes are in the state that has chance `chance`. */
    const atLeast = (need: number, total: number, chance: number): number => {
      let sum = 0;
      for (let k = need; k <= total; k++) sum += choose(total, k) * chance ** k * (1 - chance) ** (total - k);
      return sum;
    };
    const percent = (x: number) => `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(PERCENT * x)}%`;
    function draw() {
      ['n', 'r', 'w', 'f', 'x', 'p', 's', 'q', 'k'].forEach((key) => (q(`[data-${key}val]`).textContent = String(val(`[data-${key}]`))));
      const copies = val('[data-n]'), reads = Math.min(val('[data-r]'), val('[data-n]')), writes = Math.min(val('[data-w]'), val('[data-n]'));
      const down = val('[data-f]') / PERCENT, slow = val('[data-p]') / PERCENT, spares = val('[data-x]'), nodes = val('[data-s]');
      const perDay = val('[data-q]') * MILLION, keys = val('[data-k]') * MILLION;
      const data: [string, string][] = [
        ['Does R plus W exceed N, so a read overlaps the latest write?', reads + writes > copies ? 'yes' : 'no'],
        ['Unreachable nodes a write can survive with a strict quorum', String(copies - writes)],
        ['Unreachable nodes a read can survive with a strict quorum', String(copies - reads)],
        ['Chance a write succeeds, strict quorum (W of the first N)', percent(atLeast(writes, copies, 1 - down))],
        ['Chance a write succeeds, sloppy quorum (W of the first N plus spares)', percent(atLeast(writes, copies + spares, 1 - down))],
        ['Chance a read succeeds, strict quorum (R of the first N)', percent(atLeast(reads, copies, 1 - down))],
        ['Chance a read is slowed by slow replicas (more than N minus R slow)', percent(atLeast(copies - reads + 1, copies, slow))],
        ['Chance a write is slowed by slow replicas (more than N minus W slow)', percent(atLeast(copies - writes + 1, copies, slow))],
        ['Share of keys that move to a node when it joins a ring of this size', percent(1 / (nodes + 1))],
        ['Requests a day that return more than one version, at the paper’s cart shares', formatOneDecimalBelow100((perDay * CART_CONFLICT_PERCENT) / PERCENT)],
        ['Merkle tree comparisons to find one differing key in a range', formatOneDecimalBelow100(Math.ceil(Math.log2(keys)))],
        ['Rough seconds for a membership change to reach every node by gossip', formatOneDecimalBelow100(Math.ceil(Math.log2(nodes)))],
      ];
      rows.forEach((r, i) => { r.dt.textContent = data[i][0]; r.dd.textContent = data[i][1]; });
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
